     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Luis, <div><br></div><div>You can get GWAS summary statistics from many sources see bottom of this page for some of those sources: <a href=\"https://github.com/MichelNivard/GenomicSEM/wiki/2.-Important-resources-and-key-information\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/MichelNivard/GenomicSEM/wiki/2.-Important-resources-and-key-information&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237870312000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2p1cQaBl5-BWj9Iwhb5YD-\">https://github.com/MichelNivard/GenomicSEM/wiki/2.-Important-resources-and-key-information</a></div><div><br></div><div>Now if you want to know how to use plink to run a GWAS than this article is a good start: <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6001694\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6001694&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793237870312000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1uqCzD2a7heADoTKhCGebt\">https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6001694</a></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Michel</div></div>"
    ],
